\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {28}{\ignorespaces Trajectories of decision viability (\cref  {ex:viability}). (a) Five regimes in open loop: viability shares, value of identification and maximum-entropy margin; on-facet poisoning keeps $R=0$ and is seen only by the viability share. (b) Fibre dimension and Hausdorff steps: degeneration collapses the fibre to a point, and off-facet poisoning reopens it. (c) Closed loop with a window of five batches: the decision chatters inside the identified band. (d) Closed-loop decision sequences are periodic (period $W+1$ here, at most $2^W$ in general); in open loop the decision is eventually constant.}}{91}{figure.28}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:viability}{{28}{91}{Trajectories of decision viability (\cref {ex:viability}). (a) Five regimes in open loop: viability shares, value of identification and maximum-entropy margin; on-facet poisoning keeps $R=0$ and is seen only by the viability share. (b) Fibre dimension and Hausdorff steps: degeneration collapses the fibre to a point, and off-facet poisoning reopens it. (c) Closed loop with a window of five batches: the decision chatters inside the identified band. (d) Closed-loop decision sequences are periodic (period $W+1$ here, at most $2^W$ in general); in open loop the decision is eventually constant}{figure.28}{}}
\newlabel{fig:viability@cref}{{[figure][28][]28}{[1][90][]91}}
