\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {29}{\ignorespaces Three snapshots, two histories (\cref  {ex:history}). (a) The context cycle with the time at which each context arrives. At $t_1$ and $t_2$ the observed contexts form a path and the tables glue; at $t_3$ the cycle closes, and the contextual variant does not glue. (b) The interval of $P(A_0=A_1)$ over the fibre at each time (bars), with the laws selected by KL, Euclidean and TV updating (markers; blue history A, orange history B). At $t_3$ both histories have the same interval $[0.4,0.6]$; KL lands on one law, and the minimal-change rules land on opposite sides of $\tau $. (c) The $t_3$ snapshot as its last table varies with fixed margins: the interval shrinks to a point, then the fibre is empty, with contextual fraction rising from $0$, although every three contexts still glue.}}{95}{figure.29}\protected@file@percent }
