\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {37}{\ignorespaces The sources as a bundle. Top: the residual of all reports except one source, for each source (honest strands in grey, offset slightly so that tied strands stay visible), with the inspection at step $15$ dotted. Bottom: the smallest set of reports whose removal leaves the rest consistent (``none'': no set of at most three). (a) A single liar drops out of the bundle and is the suspect throughout. (b) In the cascade, the planted reports make the honest reporters $S_3$ and $R_1$ the suspects, while the smallest explanation grows from one report to more than three. (c) A lockstep coalition leaves the bundle tight until the inspection, after which the honest $S_4$ is the suspect.}}{129}{figure.37}\protected@file@percent }
