\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {50}{\ignorespaces Study 26 results. \emph  {Top left}: the projection ladder. Dark bars are exact-data ranges, light bars are estimated ranges on $\mathcal  J_z^-$ (without $\{M,C,Y\}$, per deviation D1), and circles are the truth. \emph  {Top right}: the end of two histories with the same final tables, the whole fibre, and the slice reachable by edits on $\{M,R,Y\}$. \emph  {Bottom left}: the cycle of instruments; the bars show the largest twisted-pattern sum with $3$ standard errors, against the noncontextual bound. \emph  {Bottom right}: the protection margin against twice the inspection error, and the anchor distances against the flag level.}}{195}{figure.50}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:study26results}{{50}{195}{Study 26 results. \emph {Top left}: the projection ladder. Dark bars are exact-data ranges, light bars are estimated ranges on $\mathcal J_z^-$ (without $\{M,C,Y\}$, per deviation D1), and circles are the truth. \emph {Top right}: the end of two histories with the same final tables, the whole fibre, and the slice reachable by edits on $\{M,R,Y\}$. \emph {Bottom left}: the cycle of instruments; the bars show the largest twisted-pattern sum with $3$ standard errors, against the noncontextual bound. \emph {Bottom right}: the protection margin against twice the inspection error, and the anchor distances against the flag level}{figure.50}{}}
